### [Choosing the Case]($section.id('2025-01-04T00:00:00').data('author','xq'))

I continued working on the case design with OpenSCAD.

Finding a fitting case wasn't that easy as having too much spare space
inside the case is just wasted space. After a lot of search, i've decided
to use the [Hammond RM2095L](https://www.hammfg.com/part/RM2095L) case
which suited my use case perfectly.

With the new case and more connectors, the design starts to feel alive:

> []($block.attrs('pictures'))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2025/2025-01-04_rendering1.webp').linked(true))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2025/2025-01-04_rendering2.webp').linked(true))

I also ordered the case to get a hands-on feeling for it.